  "base_address": "Defined at SoC level; offsets given relative to module base.",
  "notes": "If a future system-integration L4 is required for a Wishbone-compliant IP, the canonical 'address-side fields' to capture would be: [ADR_O()] width, [SEL_O()] width = port_size/granularity, [TGA_O()] semantics (per WISHBONE DATASHEET), [SEL_O()] -> byte-lane mapping (BIG / LITTLE ENDIAN per Section 3.5), and (for Registered Feedback) the [CTI_O()] + [BTE_O()] burst tags.",
  "rationale": "Wishbone B4 is a SoC bus / interconnect protocol, not a peripheral with a control register file. There is no MMIO register map in this document. The protocol carries the integrator-defined SLAVE address on [ADR_O()]. Concrete Wishbone-compliant IP cores define their own register files at the SoC integration level - outside this protocol spec.",
